.TH "DEPRECATIONREPORT" "3JS" "April 6, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DeprecationReport \- DeprecationReport
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]DeprecationReport\f[R] dictionary of the Reporting API
represents a deprecation report.
.PP
A deprecation report may be generated when a deprecated feature (for
example a deprecated API method) is used on a document.
Note that receiving useful deprecation reports relies on browser vendors
adding these warnings for deprecated features.
.PP
Reports of this type can be observed from within a page using a
\f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R], and a serialized version can be sent to
the default reporting server endpoint.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]body\f[R]
The body of the report.
This is an object with the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]id\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A string representing the feature or API that is deprecated, for example
\f[CR]NavigatorGetUserMedia\f[R].
This can be used to group reports by deprecated feature.
.TP
\f[B]anticipatedRemoval\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A \f[CR]Date\f[R] object (rendered as a string) representing the date
when the feature is expected to be removed from the current browser.
If the date is not known, this property will return \f[CR]null\f[R].
This value can be used to prioritize warnings.
If this property returns \f[CR]null\f[R] because the date is unknown,
then the deprecation should be considered low priority.
.TP
\f[B]message\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A string containing a human\-readable description of the deprecation,
including information such as what newer feature has superseded it, if
any.
This typically matches the message a browser will display in its
DevTools console when a deprecated feature is used, if one is available.
.TP
\f[B]sourceFile\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A string containing the path to the source file where the deprecated
feature was used, if known, or \f[CR]null\f[R] otherwise.
.TP
\f[B]lineNumber\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A number representing the line in the source file in which the
deprecated feature was used, if known, or \f[CR]null\f[R] otherwise.
.TP
\f[B]columnNumber\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
A number representing the character position in the line of the source
file in which the deprecated feature was first used, if known, or
\f[CR]null\f[R] otherwise.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
The string \f[CR]\(dqdeprecation\(dq\f[R] indicating that this is a
deprecation report.
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R]
A string representing the URL of the document that generated the report.
.SH DESCRIPTION
A deprecation report may be generated when a deprecated feature (for
example a deprecated API method) is used on a document.
.PP
You can monitor for deprecation reports within the page in which they
are triggered using the Reporting API.
To do this you create a \f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] object to listen
for reports, passing a callback method, and optionally an
\f[CR]options\f[R] property specifying the types of reports that you
want to report on.
The callback method is then called with reports of the requested types,
passing a report object.
For deprecation reports, the object will be a
\f[CR]DeprecationReport\f[R] instance (which has the \f[CR]type\f[R]
property set to \f[CR]\(dqdeprecation\(dq\f[R]).
.PP
A typical deprecation report is shown below.
Note that \f[CR]url\f[R] represents the original page that was loaded,
while \f[CR]body.sourceFile\f[R], \f[CR]body.lineNumber\f[R] and
\f[CR]body.columnNumber\f[R] indicate the specific location of the API
call that triggered the intervention (in this example they are the same
file).
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdeprecation\(dq,
  \(dqurl\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
  \(dqbody\(dq: {
    \(dqsourceFile\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
    \(dqlineNumber\(dq: 54,
    \(dqcolumnNumber\(dq: 11,
    \(dqid\(dq: \(dqXMLHttpRequestSynchronousInNonWorkerOutsideBeforeUnload\(dq,
    \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dqSynchronous \(gaXMLHttpRequest\(ga on the main thread is deprecated because of its detrimental effects to the end user\(aqs experience. For more help, check https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/.\(dq,
    \(dqanticipatedRemoval\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
  }
}
.EE
.PP
Deprecation reports are also sent as a JSON object in a \f[CR]POST\f[R]
request to the reporting server endpoint named
\f[CR]\(dqdefault\(dq\f[R], if it is defined.
The reporting server endpoint and its mapping to a particular URL are
set using the \f[CR]Reporting\-Endpoints\f[R] header.
.PP
The structure of the server report is almost exactly the same as
\f[CR]DeprecationReport\f[R], except that it additionally includes
\f[CR]age\f[R] and \f[CR]user_agent\f[R] fields.
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdeprecation\(dq,
  \(dqage\(dq: 27,
  \(dqurl\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
  \(dquser_agent\(dq: \(dqMozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:60.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/60.0\(dq,
  \(dqbody\(dq: {
    \(dqsourceFile\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
    \(dqlineNumber\(dq: 54,
    \(dqcolumnNumber\(dq: 11,
    \(dqid\(dq: \(dqXMLHttpRequestSynchronousInNonWorkerOutsideBeforeUnload\(dq,
    \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dqSynchronous \(gaXMLHttpRequest\(ga on the main thread is deprecated because of its detrimental effects to the end user\(aqs experience. For more help, check https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/.\(dq,
    \(dqanticipatedRemoval\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
  }
}
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using the \f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] interface
This example shows how to observe \f[CR]\(dqdeprecation\(dq\f[R] reports
within a page that triggers them.
.SS JavaScript
First we construct a new \f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] object to listen
for reports with the type \f[CR]\(dqdeprecation\(dq\f[R], passing a
callback that will receive and log the reports.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] options = {
  types: [\(dqdeprecation\(dq],
  buffered: \f[B]true\f[R],
};

\f[B]const\f[R] observer = \f[B]new\f[R] ReportingObserver((reports, observer) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  reports.forEach((report) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    log(JSON.stringify(report, \f[B]null\f[R], 2));
  });
}, options);

\f[I]// Start the observer\f[R]
observer.observe();
.EE
.PP
We then call the following code which uses synchronous XHR (deprecated
API).
Note that this is defined after the observer it triggers once the
observer is running.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] xhr = \f[B]new\f[R] XMLHttpRequest();
xhr.open(\(dqGET\(dq, \(dq/\(dq, \f[B]false\f[R]); \f[I]// false = synchronous (deprecated)\f[R]
xhr.send();
.EE
.SS Results
On browsers that support deprecation reports, a report should be
displayed below.
Note that the \f[CR]type\f[R] is \f[CR]\(dqdeprecation\(dq\f[R].
.SS Sending a report to a reporting endpoint
Configuring a web page to send a deprecation report requires that you
set a reporting server endpoint named \(lqdefault\(rq using the
\f[CR]Reporting\-Endpoints\f[R] header.
Below we set the \f[CR]default\f[R] endpoint to
\f[CR]https://example.com/deprecation\f[R]:
.PP
The report will then be sent as a JSON object in a \f[CR]POST\f[R]
request to the endpoint whenever a deprecated API is used.
It has the same structure as \f[CR]DeprecationReport\f[R], except for
the addition of \f[CR]age\f[R] and \f[CR]user_agent\f[R] properties.
.IP
.EX
[
  {
    \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqdeprecation\(dq,
    \(dqage\(dq: 27,
    \(dqurl\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
    \(dquser_agent\(dq: \(dqMozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:60.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/60.0\(dq,
    \(dqbody\(dq: {
      \(dqsourceFile\(dq: \(dqhttps://example.com/\(dq,
      \(dqlineNumber\(dq: 54,
      \(dqcolumnNumber\(dq: 11,
      \(dqid\(dq: \(dqXMLHttpRequestSynchronousInNonWorkerOutsideBeforeUnload\(dq,
      \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dqSynchronous \(gaXMLHttpRequest\(ga on the main thread is deprecated because of its detrimental effects to the end user\(aqs experience. For more help, check https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/.\(dq,
      \(dqanticipatedRemoval\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
    }
  }
]
.EE
